Feature: Customer dropdown # features/home_page.feature:1
  As a user opening the home page
  I want to see a customer dropdown
  So that I can select a customer
  Scenario: Default option shows "Select Customer"          # features/home_page.feature:6
    Given the app is running                                # steps/home_steps.py:81
    When I open the home page                               # steps/home_steps.py:91
    Then the customer dropdown default is "Select Customer" # steps/home_steps.py:97

  Scenario: Customer dropdown is rendered and functional    # features/home_page.feature:10
    Given I am on the home page                             # steps/home_steps.py:85
    When I click the customer dropdown                      # steps/home_steps.py:144
    Then the dropdown should be visible and contain options # steps/home_steps.py:152

  @api
  Scenario: Customer dropdown is populated from API and selection persists  # features/home_page.feature:16
    Given I am on the home page                                             # steps/home_steps.py:85
    When I wait for the customer dropdown to be populated from the API      # steps/home_steps.py:109
    And I select the first available customer                               # steps/home_steps.py:114
    Then the selected customer remains selected in the dropdown             # steps/home_steps.py:136

Feature: Manage Orders page # features/manage_orders.feature:1
  As a user on the Manage Orders page
  I want to view my order history
  So that I can track my purchases
  Background:   # features/manage_orders.feature:6

  Scenario: Manage Orders page displays the correct heading  # features/manage_orders.feature:11
    Given the app is running                                 # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                                # steps/home_steps.py:85
    Given I select the first customer from the dropdown      # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:65
    And I navigate to "Manage Orders"                        # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then the manage orders heading should be visible         # steps/manage_orders_steps.py:55

  @api
  Scenario: Empty state is shown when no orders are available  # features/manage_orders.feature:17
    Given the app is running                                   # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                                  # steps/home_steps.py:85
    Given I select the first customer from the dropdown        # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:65
    And I navigate to "Manage Orders"                          # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    Then the empty orders message should be visible            # steps/manage_orders_steps.py:66

  @api
  Scenario: Empty state has a link that navigates to Purchase Rings  # features/manage_orders.feature:23
    Given the app is running                                         # steps/home_steps.py:81
    And I am on the home page                                        # steps/home_steps.py:85
    Given I select the first customer from the dropdown              # steps/purchase_rings_steps.py:65
    And I navigate to "Manage Orders"                                # steps/navigation_steps.py:71
    And the empty orders message is visible                          # steps/manage_orders_steps.py:77
    When I click the Start Shopping link                             # steps/manage_orders_steps.py:85
    Then I should be on the "Purchase Rings" page                    # steps/navigation_steps.py:99

  @api
  Scenario: Order cards are displayed when the API returns data  # features/manage_orders.feature:31
